#
# # Rule 02 — Mintlify writing standards
#
# ## Contract
#
# This rule owns the `docs/**` Mintlify documentation surface: writing style, MDX structure, navigation, component usage, accessibility, and docs validation. Long component examples belong in the Mintlify skill/reference files, not this rule.
#
# ## Writing rules
#
# - Write for the user's task, not for product promotion.
# - Use clear, direct second-person instructions.
# - Use active voice and present tense for current behavior.
# - Lead with the most important information.
# - Put prerequisites before steps and expected results after meaningful steps.
# - Use progressive disclosure: common/basic workflows first, advanced or rare details later.
# - Avoid promotional, vague, and editorial phrasing such as "rich heritage," "it is important to note," "this article will," and uncited "industry reports suggest."
# - Use descriptive, keyword-rich, sentence-case headings.
# - Avoid emoji and decorative formatting. Bold only when it helps the reader perform an action.
#
# ## ADHD-first scanability
#
# - Give each page one job and make that job clear in the first paragraph.
# - Lead with the task, command, or outcome the reader came for; move background below the first action.
# - Keep paragraphs short. Prefer one idea per paragraph and use tables or components only when they reduce scanning work.
# - Use progressive disclosure: the common path first, details and edge cases later.
# - Non-hub pages should have one primary next-action or related-resource grid. Hub pages may have multiple grids when each grid owns a distinct choice set.
# - Body headings use sentence case unless the heading is a command, acronym, code symbol, product name, or diagnostic code.
#
# ## Page and navigation rules
#
# - Every docs page uses `.mdx`.
# - Every page starts with frontmatter containing `title`, `description`, and `keywords`.
# - Do not add an in-body H1. Mintlify owns the page H1 from frontmatter; start sections at H2.
# - Use kebab-case filenames.
# - Public pages must be present in `docs/docs.json` navigation.
# - Pages intentionally omitted from navigation use `hidden: true`; omit `hidden` instead of setting `false`.
# - Internal docs links are extensionless and root-relative, such as `/configuration/hints`.
# - Do not use `.md`, `.mdx`, repo-relative `docs/...`, or absolute `supaschema.com/docs/...` links for internal Mintlify navigation.
# - When moving or renaming a page, update navigation and add a redirect in the same change.
# - Use `docs/.mintignore` only for drafts, private generated assets, or stray non-content files; do not hide public pages there.
#
# ## MDX and component rules
#
# - Use Mintlify components for the structures they own: `<Steps>` for complex procedures, `<ParamField>` for parameters/flags, `<ResponseField>` and `<Expandable>` for response shapes, `<Frame>` for images, and semantic callouts for notes, tips, warnings, and critical cautions.
# - Command/reference pages with flags or options document them with `<ParamField>`.
# - Images live under `docs/images/**`, use root-relative `/images/**` paths, include descriptive alt text, and are wrapped in `<Frame>`.
# - Code fences must include a language tag and filename/title when useful.
# - Use `text` for terminal output, object keys, ASCII diagrams, and plain output.
# - Never carry rendered-output artifacts such as `theme={null}` on code fences.
# - Use realistic placeholders and never include API keys or secrets.
# - Public API pages prefer OpenAPI/AsyncAPI from `docs/docs.json`; manual endpoint docs must include request/response examples and structured fields.
# - Comparison pages under `docs/comparisons/` must include `Last verified YYYY-MM-DD` for external claims and a `## Sources` section with at least one outbound source link.
#
# ## AI and MCP readiness
#
# - Keep Mintlify agent-readiness surfaces enabled where the product docs describe them: `llms.txt`, `llms-full.txt`, `skill.md`, and read-only docs MCP/search surfaces.
# - Reverse proxies must forward `/mcp`, `/authed/mcp`, `/skill.md`, `/.well-known/mcp*`, `/.well-known/skills/*`, and `/.well-known/agent-skills/*` when proxying the docs site.
# - Hidden pages are excluded from search, sitemap, and AI context unless intentionally indexed by the docs config.
#
# ## Verification
#
# For docs changes, run the narrowest docs check first, then broaden when navigation, components, links, generated docs, screenshots, or agent-readiness surfaces changed.
#
# ```bash
# npm run docs:lint
# npm run docs:check
# ```
#
# Preview with `mint dev` when page structure, navigation, or components changed.
#
# ## Failure behavior
#
# Fix docs lint, Mintlify validation, broken links, missing navigation entries, heading hierarchy, component syntax, and accessibility failures at the source page or `docs/docs.json`. Do not hide public pages in `.mintignore` to make validation pass.
#
# ## Done means
#
# - Changed pages have valid frontmatter.
# - Navigation and redirects are current.
# - Code examples are syntactically valid or explicitly verified.
# - Images have alt text and `<Frame>` wrappers.
# - `docs:check` evidence exists for material docs changes.
#
